Z||000002||Fret Naught||05-08-2000||12:48 AM||||Thanks GTGIRL, I checked it out they want 20 BUCKS!!!, silly me, I thought I could get the info for free. I guess I am just to cheap no thrifty to purchase the info. I love what they tell you yes we have information on your car, could be a good report like no news is good news or it could be bad just send up 19.95 for a full report. I don't know seems kind of sneaky to me.||||reg||12
Z||000003||LarryB||05-08-2000||01:10 AM||||Carfax doesn't check for recall work, they check title and registration/inspection info for things like possible odometer rollback, title washing to hide a salvage or lemon law buyback, etc. <P>To check for recall work have your VIN number in hand and call 1-800-PMCARES, but you may have to bring the car to the local Pontiac dealer and ask them to physically inspect the car to verify the recall work was done.||||reg||1
